Serve the web client behind a trusted proxy with no pairing prompt

Stock `orca serve` delivers its pairing token only in the URL fragment, but a
Coder tile URL is fixed at template-build time, so a stock tile lands on a
"paste a pairing code" form.

Trusted mode binds the runtime WS listener to loopback and treats that bind as
proof the proxy already authenticated. The credential cannot simply be omitted:
an Orca pairing offer carries `publicKeyB64` alongside `deviceToken` and is the
channel's key material rather than an authorisation check, so `WebRuntimeClient`
cannot be constructed without it. Delivery moves from the URL fragment to a
loopback-gated `GET /trusted-session`; `createPairingOffer` is reused unmodified,
so E2EE is intact. The client dials same-origin from `window.location`, so the
tile needs no `--pairing-address`, and on `auth-failed` it re-probes and adopts a
new offer.

The route resolves through upstream's own `mapProxyPrefixedStaticPathname`, the
mapper that already forwards a reverse proxy's path prefix for `/web-index.html`
and `/assets/`: the client probes `new URL('trusted-session', location.href)`, so
a page served under a path-forwarding proxy asks for `/<prefix>/trusted-session`
and an exact match alone would 404 it back to the paste form. The mapping is
added after the asset branch, never before, so a credential is still unreachable
from under `/assets/`. Loopback, not the path shape, is the gate.

The offer is minted with `reach: 'this-computer'`. It shares one pending runtime
device with the "Share this Orca server" grant, and `getOrCreatePendingDevice`
widens reach but never narrows it, so an omitted reach would silently re-widen
what that grant just pinned and let the next reconnect bind every interface
(STA-2370). The `--trusted-proxy` loopback bind and the `ensureNetworkExposure`
guard both stay as defence in depth: `createMobilePairingOffer` calls
`ensureNetworkExposure` unconditionally, before its `local-only` branch, so it is
this patch's guard that keeps the web tile's mobile pairing from publishing the
runtime on every interface.

To test, open the workspace tile: the full Orca web UI should load with no
pairing prompt; repeat behind a path-forwarding proxy. Covered by
`static-web-client-handler.test.ts` - the endpoint serves the offer with
`Cache-Control: no-store` to a loopback peer, 404s a non-loopback one, 503s
before an offer can be minted, answers a forwarded `/<prefix>/trusted-session`,
still 404s `/assets/foo/trusted-session`, answers `HEAD` with headers and no
body, and is absent entirely when trusted-proxy mode is off - and by
`trusted-session-pairing-reach.test.ts` for the shared pending device's reach.
